§§ `The person, the entity and another person (a / the / another; assumed, not ruled, 2026-10-27)`

-- The knowing offences are regulative rules whose condition is `the prohibition binds the person`, which now requires that the other person differs from the person making the statement.  The statements are those of
-- g7-tests-fixtures-expressions (`scenario NN, case K`).  i: the maker means to mislead only themself, so the rule is not live (FULFILLED even though the event is the forbidden act); i-entity: the same with the entity as the maker;
-- ii: the maker is the entity itself and the other person a donor (Articles 21(7), 23(5)): live, BREACH; iii: a third person and a donor: BREACH; vi: a party equal to the maker, built again: not live.
-- The (b) rules (cause or permit another person to refer) are not changed: the act they forbid is by its name the entity causing ANOTHER person to refer, and the first traces of this module use them with statements whose
-- maker is the entity, so a condition on the maker there would change those answers; the Boolean forms of the (b) limbs carry the condition (g7-tests-expressions, section `The person, the entity and another person`).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 21(2) a person must not say that an unregistered entity is registered, with knowledge and intent` `a person other than the entity` `a Jersey entity` FALSE `scenario 06, case i` AT 0 WITH
